{{Short description|Ultra-faint dwarf galaxy on the Aquarius constellation}}
{{Infobox galaxy|name=Aquarius lll|constellation name=[[Aquarius (constellation)|Aquarius]]|dist_ly=277,232 ly|type=[[Dwarf galaxy]]|notes=Metal poor stars|image=Astronomers Discover Dizzying Spin of the Milky Way Galaxy’s “Halo” (28543855025).jpg|caption=Artistic illustration of the halo of the [[Milky Way galaxy]] which Aquarius lll is located in}}
{{Use dmy dates|date=August 2025}}

'''Aquarius lll''' is an ultra-faint satellite [[dwarf galaxy]] located in the outer [[Galactic halo|halo]] around 85 kiloparsecs from the [[Milky Way|Milky Way galaxy]] in the [[constellation]] of [[Aquarius (constellation)|Aquarius]]. The [[star]]s within Aquarius lll are extremely [[Metal-poor|metal poor]].<ref name=":0">{{Citation |last1=Cerny |first1=W. |title=Discovery and Spectroscopic Confirmation of Aquarius III: A Low-Mass Milky Way Satellite Galaxy |date=1 October 2024 |arxiv=2410.00981 |last2=Chiti |first2=A. |last3=Geha |first3=M. |last4=Mutlu-Pakdil |first4=B. |last5=Drlica-Wagner |first5=A. |last6=Tan |first6=C. Y. |last7=Adamów |first7=M. |last8=Pace |first8=A. B. |last9=Simon |first9=J. D. |journal=The Astrophysical Journal |volume=979 |issue=2 |page=164 |doi=10.3847/1538-4357/ad8eba |doi-access=free |bibcode=2025ApJ...979..164C }}</ref> It could have at least one [[RR Lyrae variable|RR Lyrae star]].<ref>{{Cite journal |last1=Ngeow |first1=Chow-Choong |last2=Bhardwaj |first2=Anupam |date=March 2025 |title=Candidate RR Lyrae Associated with the Ultrafaint Dwarf Galaxy Aquarius III |journal=The Astronomical Journal |language=en |volume=169 |issue=3 |pages=156 |doi=10.3847/1538-3881/adadf1 |bibcode=2025AJ....169..156N |doi-access=free |issn=0004-6256}}</ref>

The [[galaxy]] is possibly on its first in fall to the galaxy. Notably, unlike other [[Satellite galaxy|satellite galaxies]] orbiting the Milky Way galaxy, it had not experienced significant [[Tidal force|tidal disruption]] from the [[Galactic disc|galactic disk]].<ref name=":0" />

